@@ -11,3 +11,9 @@ Rendered scans run through `/page/:sectionID/rendered-scan`, which resolves the
 A reviewer can sign only after all criteria for all listed pages are current and verified. The statement binds to a digest of scope, page fingerprints and review records. Scope/content/rendering changes invalidate it. Exported reports are dated evidence snapshots, not promises about future content or a third-party certification. Changes outside the application are detected on rescan; scan freshness limits this gap.
 
 Human tests must cover mathematical meaning and navigability, duplicate announcements, keyboard interaction, zoom/reflow/text spacing, media and complex images, linguistic accuracy, and the complete reader processes defined in scope. Never auto-populate these results from AI inference or axe checks.
+
+## Remediation delivery acceptance
+
+The panel also supports a separate remediation handoff sign-off. `POST /conformance/remediation_signoff` accepts the current delivery with outstanding findings explicitly retained. Shared reader accessibility and human screen-reader/keyboard/manual testing are listed as independent deferred projects. These do not block delivery acceptance. This record never changes WCAG results, verifies queue tasks, or claims accessibility conformance.
+
+Delivery acceptance requires a defined scope, current source scans for all listed pages, a statement and explicit acknowledgement of the deferred work. The server binds the authenticated actor, evidence digest, outstanding counts and fixed deferred scope; clients cannot erase those disclosures. Content, scope and evidence changes invalidate matching acceptance, and source scan freshness is 24 hours. The combined export includes both delivery acceptance and the independent conformance status.
